# two_rooms_doorway_scan.rish -- forward-facing pages name their room at the door.
#
# Native orchestration -- per-file verdict in two_rooms_doorway_scan_one.sh
# (stamp compare, head-25 Status, case-insensitive room register).
#
# WHAT CHANGED 20260906, and why the numbers moved. The roster beside this file was a shell glob
# over three rooms; `active-designing/` folded to `date/YYYYMMDD/` and a shell `*` stops at `/`,
# so 607 pages left the reach with nothing to say so. The roster reads `git ls-files` now, whose
# pathspec `*` crosses `/`. Reach 319 -> 972 files, 216 -> 880 post-seating pages, and three
# pages that name no room became visible for the first time since their room folded.
#
# THE REACH FLOOR, and what it is for. A gate held at zero cannot tell a clean collection from a
# dead instrument, since both answer zero (REDS %416). Three floors stand below, and the third is
# this defect class watching for its own return: at least one page must come from a `date/` shelf.
# Should a roster narrow to the flat room again -- a rewritten glob, a room renamed -- the folded
# count falls to zero and this refuses, where the elder simply reported a smaller clean tree.
#
# WHAT IS RATCHETED RATHER THAN GATED. Forty-five pages carry a Status that names no room, or no
# Status at all. Three of them sit on `date/` shelves and are dated testimony, which
# accrete-never-break keeps exactly as written -- so a hard gate at zero could never close, and a
# gate that can never close is one somebody turns off. The ceiling only falls, and every failing
# page is named on every pass, so a repair is one line away from the reading that found it.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_scan.rish

let seating_env = env "TWO_ROOMS_SEATING_STAMP"
let seating = "20260705-203144"
if seating_env != "" then let seating = seating_env

# The ceiling only ever falls FROM WHAT IT PUBLISHES. Measured 20260906.161500 on the repaired
# roster at 45 -- 42 pages already inside the elder reach, plus 3 the fold had hidden since
# active-designing folded. It publishes at 46, because the lap that measured 45 died before its
# commit and one external-research page landed in the gap; a number measured on a tree that has
# since moved is REDS %341's class, and the honest reading is the one taken at the send.
#
# IT ARRIVED RED AND FELL TO 44 (`20260907.001500`). The 46 was measured on a 972-page tree at
# `20260906.161500` and published on a 974-page tree seven hours later, by which time a third
# `Proposed` page had landed and the reading stood at **47** -- a ratchet rostered at a ceiling its
# own tree already exceeded, which is a guard that reds on arrival. That is this scan's own header
# reasoning turned on itself: a number measured before the send and landed after is a number about
# a tree that has moved.
#
# The repair is not a wider gate. Three pages read `**Status:** Proposed -- external research`, and
# TWO_ROOMS.md's gloss table names four tokens -- checkable, vision, mixed, research for
# understanding -- with `proposed` among none of them, while its own prose says "what is proven as
# proven and what is proposed as proposed". Each of the three already NAMED its register in its own
# next sentence: two say the numbers are witness-bound and the design reading is proposed, which is
# `mixed` by the table's own gloss, and the third says nothing here binds a witness, which is
# `research for understanding`. So each Status gained the token its own sentence already asserted --
# no claim changed, three pages started naming their room, and the reading fell 47 to 44. Whether
# `proposed` should itself be a fifth token is still the canon's to settle rather than this
# guard's, and it is carried on the card.
#
# AND IT ROSE AGAIN OVERNIGHT, 44 -> 48, WHICH IS THE FINDING (`20260907.094712`). Four of the four
# new pages were written by hands that had read the law -- two of them cite `context/TWO_ROOMS.md`
# in the very Status line that names no room. The transcription repair above had then been done
# twice in two days and regrown twice, so the missing piece is at WRITE time rather than at census
# time; `tools/f/fleet_baton.txt` carries the one clause now, which is where a habit reaches every
# ship on its next lap.
#
# THE READING FELL 48 -> 37 IN THREE MOVES, and each is a different kind of thing:
#   +4 free -- the door is the HEAD, not one key. Nine pages answered under `**Room:**` rather than
#      `**Status:**`, two of them spelling `Mixed`, and were read as naming no room at all.
#   -3 caught -- the token is a WORD, not a substring. `no infrastructure provisioned`,
#      `no VPS provisioned` and `divisional roles` each carry the letters of `vision`, and three
#      post-seating pages were passing on them. `visionary` is kept, since `Visionary room` is an
#      honest naming that two pages write.
#   +11 repaired -- each page's own next sentence already said its register, transcribed into the
#      door line. No claim changed on any of them.
#
# THE RATCHET REACHED ITS FLOOR, 38 -> 3 (`20260907.191211`), and the floor is structural rather
# than tidy. The reading arrived RED at 38 against a ceiling of 37 -- one page had landed overnight,
# which is what a zero-slack ceiling does over a population that grows. Twenty-nine living pages
# were repaired the same way the +11 move above was: each page's own opening sentence already
# asserted its register, and the token was transcribed into its door line beside whatever else that
# line said. No claim changed on any of them, and the commonest honest answer was `mixed` -- a
# design essay reasoning from measured readings toward a proposal is both registers by construction,
# which is why `mixed` is also the most-written token in the tree (334 of 846 post-seating door
# lines, measured this lap).
#
# THE THREE THAT REMAIN CAN NEVER BE REPAIRED, and that is the point. All three sit on
# `active-designing/date/20260820/`, and dated testimony keeps every word it wrote
# (accrete-never-break). So 3 is a floor rather than a target, and the ceiling stands there: from
# here the guard's whole remaining job is catching pages written from now on.
#
# WHICH MAKES IT A GATE ON NEW WRITING, WEARING A RATCHET'S CLOTHES, and the difference decides
# where the repair belongs. A ratchet reports a backlog somebody works down; this now reds the whole
# fleet the first time any hand writes a door line without a token. It runs at `tier cadence`, so
# the hand that wrote the page is not the hand that meets the refusal -- a stranger meets it, up to
# five rounds later, and repairs somebody else's door. That is the shape the census has already
# regrown from twice.
#
# THE WRITE-TIME REACH TAKEN THIS LAP is the room's own front door rather than a hook.
# `active-designing/README.md` gained a *The room at the door* section on `20260907.015907` and has
# had no silent page since; `external-research/README.md` recorded teaching the token in its own
# `Last updated` line on the same stamp and left its body silent, and the one page that landed
# between then and now came from that room. Its *How To Add an Exploration* ritual -- the list a
# writer actually reads before adding a page -- now carries the token. Sample size one, said
# plainly; the mechanism is what recommends it, not the count. `docs/README.md` is untouched: it
# supplies 14 pages, none of them silent, and it stands at the 40 lines it declares.
#
# WHAT A GREP STILL CANNOT READ, named rather than guessed at: a token can be DENIED and still
# match. `**Room:** Proposed -- nothing here is checkable until a witness binds it` read OK on the
# word its own sentence negates. That page is repaired at the source, and a negation heuristic is
# declined here -- `not vision -- checkable` is honest prose and a rule refusing it would refuse
# more truth than it caught. Presence is what a grep reads; assertion stays a reader's.
# THE ROSTER READ THREE ROOMS AND THE TREE SHIPS FIVE (20260908). `docs-geode/` -- the shipping
# shelf, the room whose whole job is the page a stranger meets first -- stood outside this guard
# for its entire life, and `docs-geode/README.md` names "three prose rooms" that overlap this
# roster's three in exactly one. The room joins at zero cost: 10 pages, 0 silent, because the one
# genre here that stamps its basenames is the blog and its first piece already reads `mixed`.
# `manual/` JOINED THE NEXT LAP (20260908), by being repaired rather than by a ceiling moving.
# Its 7 silent pages each carried an honest `**Status:**` line that answered the lifecycle question
# and never the register one; the token was added beside what each already said, judged from the
# page -- four `mixed`, three `checkable`. The room reads 29 pages and 0 silent, so it entered on
# `docs-geode/`'s own terms.
# `foundations/` JOINED THE SAME WAY (20260908), and it was the larger half of the bill: 83 pages,
# 35 silent, each read and given the token its own page earns -- 23 `mixed`, 12 `vision`. Two of the
# 35 answer under `**Room:**` rather than `**Status:**`, because their Status sentence runs onto a
# second line and this scan keeps the first, so an appended token would land mid-clause. The second
# key, seated 20260907, is what let those two be repaired without rewriting a paragraph to suit a
# grep. `context/` (105 pages, 38 silent) stays out: one more lap of the same shape.
#
# `starts-with "docs/"` does NOT catch a `docs-geode/` path -- the prefixes part at the fourth
# character -- so the two rooms are counted apart and neither borrows the other's reach leg. That
# was checked rather than assumed, because a reach leg passing on a sibling room's pages is the
# same silent-narrowing shape this whole family was built for.
#
let ceiling_env = env "TWO_ROOMS_DOORWAY_CEILING"
let ceiling = "3"
if ceiling_env != "" then let ceiling = ceiling_env

# THE EXEMPTION WAS POINTED AT THE LIVING PAGES (20260911). `scan_one` passed any page whose
# basename carries no one-clock stamp, calling it grandfathered. The mark law reads that same
# absence the other way -- *a file whose own basename carries a one-clock stamp is testimony, and
# everything else is living* -- so the clause freed `context/LEXICON.md`, the `manual/` guides and
# the `docs-geode/` tutorials, and gated three pages of dated testimony nobody may ever repair.
#
# Measured the lap this reading landed: 1,254 pages, of which 138 carry no stamp and 106 of those
# named no room. The roster's own comments read `manual/ 29 pages and 0 silent` and `foundations/
# 83 pages and 0 silent`, and both zeros were true of the population the guard could see. Sixteen
# were repaired the same lap -- 13 `context/specs/`, one design shape, one foundation, one
# external-research canon -- so the ceiling opens at 90. The remainder, by room: 33
# `active-designing/`, 23 `context/`, 20 `manual/`, 9 `docs-geode/`, 6 in the lineage silo.
#
# TWO NUMBERS RATHER THAN ONE, because a page never changes class: a stamp is in a basename or it
# is not. Merging them would let a repair in one class hide a regression in the other, and the
# dated ratchet's floor of 3 is structural where this one's is zero.
let living_ceiling_env = env "TWO_ROOMS_LIVING_CEILING"
let living_ceiling = "90"
if living_ceiling_env != "" then let living_ceiling = living_ceiling_env

let roster = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_roster.sh"]
assert roster.ok else "two_rooms doorway roster failed"
let files = where (lines roster.out) as p: p != ""

let from_research = where files as f: f starts-with "external-research/"
let from_designing = where files as f: f starts-with "active-designing/"
let from_docs = where files as f: f starts-with "docs/"
let from_geode = where files as f: f starts-with "docs-geode/"
let from_manual = where files as f: f starts-with "manual/"
let from_foundations = where files as f: f starts-with "foundations/"
let from_context = where files as f: f starts-with "context/"
let from_shelves = where files as f: f contains "/date/"

let results = map files as f: run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/two_rooms_doorway_scan_one.sh" f seating]

for-each results as r do say trim r.out

let fails = where results as r: r.ok == false
let living_silent = where results as r: (trim r.out) starts-with "LIVING-SILENT"
let stampless = where results as r: r.out contains "no one-clock stamp"

say "doorway pages=${length files} research=${length from_research} designing=${length from_designing} docs=${length from_docs} geode=${length from_geode} manual=${length from_manual} foundations=${length from_foundations} context=${length from_context} folded=${length from_shelves}"
say "doorway fails=${length fails} ceiling=${ceiling} seating=${seating}"
say "doorway stampless=${length stampless} living_silent=${length living_silent} living_ceiling=${living_ceiling}"

if length from_research == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: external-research read no page"
if length from_designing == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: active-designing read no page"
if length from_docs == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: docs read no page"
if length from_geode == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: docs-geode read no page"
if length from_manual == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: manual read no page"
if length from_foundations == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: foundations read no page"
if length from_context == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: context read no page"
if length from_shelves == 0 then say "FAIL doorway reach: no folded page read -- a glob has narrowed to the flat room again"

if length from_research == 0 then exit 1
if length from_designing == 0 then exit 1
if length from_docs == 0 then exit 1
if length from_geode == 0 then exit 1
if length from_manual == 0 then exit 1
if length from_foundations == 0 then exit 1
if length from_context == 0 then exit 1
if length from_shelves == 0 then exit 1

let under = run ["sh" "-c" "test ${length fails} -le ${ceiling}"]

if under.ok == false then say "FAIL doorway ratchet: ${length fails} pages name no room, above the ceiling of ${ceiling}"
if under.ok == false then exit 1

let living_under = run ["sh" "-c" "test ${length living_silent} -le ${living_ceiling}"]

if living_under.ok == false then say "FAIL doorway living ratchet: ${length living_silent} living pages name no room, above the ceiling of ${living_ceiling}"
if living_under.ok == false then exit 1

say "verdict=ok"
say "OK   doorway scan complete (seating ${seating})"
